0. Definitions

   "Materials"  Everything in this repository authored by the copyright holder
                (MCP servers, bootstrap, baselines, documentation, curriculum
                design). Third-party components are excluded — see Section 5.

   "Output"     Works, code, images, sound, or documents you create using the
                Materials.

   "Instructional Use"  Using the Materials, in whole or in part, as the
                teaching material or curriculum basis of a course, workshop,
                class, or educational program offered to others — whether or
                not a fee is charged, and whether or not for profit.

1. Permitted

   You may use, copy, and modify the Materials for personal purposes,
   including study, experimentation, and your own creative work.

2. Output is unrestricted

   No restriction in this license applies to Output created using the
   Materials. Rights in Output belong to the person who made it. Exhibiting,
   selling, distributing, or commercially exploiting Output requires no
   permission from the copyright holder.

3. Restricted

   Without prior written permission from the copyright holder, you may not:

   (a) engage in Instructional Use;
   (b) sell the Materials, incorporate them into a paid product or service,
       or otherwise generate revenue from them;
   (c) distribute derivative works that substantially substitute for the
       Materials, for the purposes in (a) or (b).

4. Permitted notwithstanding Section 3

   Section 3 does not restrict:

   (a) attributed quotation, linking, and screenshots;
   (b) mention and demonstration in talks and presentations;
   (c) one-off sharing between individuals;
   (d) criticism, research, and news reporting.

5. Third-party components

   This repository may include components copyrighted by others (official
   example code, libraries, assets). Those parts remain governed by their
   original licenses; this license neither alters nor narrows them.
   See NOTICE.md for the list and terms.

6. Requesting permission

   If you want to do something in Section 3, get in touch. It is a matter for
   discussion, not a categorical no.

       Bae Joonhyung  jh.bae@kaist.ac.kr
       https://opencircuit.club

7. No warranty

   The Materials are provided "as is", without warranty of any kind, express
   or implied, including merchantability, fitness for a particular purpose,
   and non-infringement. The copyright holder is not liable for any damages
   arising from use of the Materials.

8. Governing law

   The laws of the Republic of Korea.
